#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:114
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[bull-ogres,†1]]1. Bull Ogres"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:120
msgid ""
"If an Ogre unit can use its initiative to charge an enemy unit of humans at "
"the start of the Command phase then it must do so. This happens "
"automatically and their commander can do nothing about it. ‘Humans’ "
"encompasses all men including Chaos Warriors and Marauders, but not Dwarfs, "
"Elves etc."
msgstr ""
"Si une unité d’Ogres peut utiliser son initiative pour charger une unité d’"
"humains (littéralement humains… ce qui inclut les Guerriers et Maraudeurs du "
"Chaos, mais pas les Nains, les Elfes et autres humanoïdes) au début de la "
"phase d’Ordres, elle doit le faire, quels que soient les désirs de leur "
"commandant."

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:121
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[leadbelchers,†2]]2. Leadbelchers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:124
msgid ""
"Leadbelchers’ cannons have a range of 15cm.  Leadbelchers’ shooting attacks "
"impose a −1 penalty to armour rolls."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:125
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[yhetees,†3]]3. Yhetees"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:128
msgid ""
"If the unit of Yhetees charges against an enemy in the open it receives an "
"additional +1 Attack modifier in the same way as chariots and monsters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:133
msgid ""
"A Yhetee unit can only give support and be supported by other Yhetee units, "
"must pursue retreating enemies where possible and must advance into a combat "
"if they are able to do so."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[gnoblars,†4]]4. Gnoblars"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:136
msgid ""
"This unit is allowed to shoot as if it had bows but its range is reduced to "
"15cm."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:141
msgid ""
"A Gnoblar stand cannot be supported by other kinds of infantry – only by "
"other Gnoblar stands. Note, however, that Gnoblars can support other kinds "
"of infantry as normal."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:143
msgid "Gnoblars cannot be given magic items."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:146
msgid "Characters cannot join Gnoblar units."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:147
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[gorgers,†5]]5. Gorgers"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:152
msgid ""
"When trying to issue an order to a unit of Gorgers or to a brigade that "
"contains a unit of Gorgers, there is always a −1 Command penalty due their "
"beastly and unruly nature. Gorgers always ignore distance modifiers when "
"receiving orders and can pursue any type of retreating enemy."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:175
msgid ""
"Gorgers do not have to be deployed before the game if the player does not "
"wish to do so.  Instead individual units can be infiltrated onto the "
"battlefield once the game has begun. To infiltrate a unit, the Ogre player "
"nominates the point where he wants the Gorgers to appear and issues an "
"‘infiltration’ order from any character. The character does not have to be "
"within his normal command range to issue an infiltration order – the "
"character’s command range is considered to extend over the entire tabletop "
"when issuing an infiltration order. Treat the order as issued to the "
"nominated point, and apply the Gorgers’ standard −1 command penalty and any "
"modifiers for proximity of enemy. The nominated point must lie either on the "
"table within dense terrain or on any base edge other than the enemy player’s "
"own table edge. If successful, place one stand on the nominated spot and "
"arrange the rest of the unit into formation around it. The infiltrated unit "
"cannot be placed so that it touches an enemy unit. Once deployed, orders can "
"be given to the unit by the same character that gave the infiltration order. "
"The infiltrating unit is considered to have used its first order to deploy. "
"If the infiltration order is failed the unit is not deployed and cannot "
"infiltrate that turn, it can attempt to infiltrate in a subsequent turn at "
"the same or a different place."
msgstr ""
"Une unité de Cannibales n'a pas à être déployée au début de la bataille si "
"le joueur le désire. À la place, l’unité peut s’infiltrer sur le champ de "
"bataille une fois la partie commencée. Pour infiltrer une unité, le joueur "
"Ogre désigne le point où il veut la faire apparaître et doit lui donner un "
"ordre d’infiltration avec l’un de ses personnages. Le personnage ne tient "
"pas compte des portées d’ordre pour donner l’ordre d’infiltration : on "
"considère que sa portée d’ordre s’étend à l’ensemble du champ de bataille "
"pour ce qui est de donner un tel ordre. Considérez que l’ordre est donné au "
"point où l’unité doit apparaître, et appliquez les malus de -1 au "
"commandement des Cannibales et de proximité de l’ennemi.  Le point d’"
"apparition de l'unité doit être situé en terrain dense ou sur un bord de "
"table n’étant pas celui du joueur adverse. Si l’ordre d’infiltration est "
"donné avec succès, placez un socle de l’unité sur le point indiqué et "
"positionnez les autres en formation autour de celui-ci. L’unité infiltrée ne "
"peut pas être placée de façon à toucher l’ennemi. Une fois qu’elle est "
"déployée, elle peut recevoir des ordres du personnage qui a donné l’ordre d’"
"infiltration, si celui-ci se trouve à portée d’ordre habituelle : on "
"considère qu’elle a utilisé son premier ordre pour se déployer. Si l’ordre d’"
"infiltration est un échec, l’unité n’est pas déployée et ne peut pas s’"
"infiltrer lors de ce tour. Elle pourra essayer de nouveau lors d’un tour "
"suivant, au même endroit ou en un autre lieu."

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:177
msgid "Gorgers don’t suffer the usual −1 Command penalty for Dense Terrain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:178
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[rhinox-riders,†6]]6. Rhinox Riders"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:180
msgid "Units of Rhinox Riders are unaffected by terror."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:183
msgid ""
"Rhinox Riders receive +1 Attack when charging against an enemy in open in "
"the same way as chariots and monsters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:184
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[slave-giant,†7]]7. Slave Giant"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:187
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[scrap-launcher,†8]]8. Scrap Launcher"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:189
msgid ""
"Scrap Launcher is a xref:rules:artillery-and-machines.adoc#stone-"
"thrower[Stone Thrower] as described in the Warmaster Rulebook."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:190
#, no-wrap
msgid "[[bull-rhinox,†9]]9. Bull Rhinox"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:192
msgid "Tyrants, Bruisers and Butchers may ride the Bull Rhinox."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:195
msgid ""
"A unit that is joined with a character mounted on this huge beast causes "
"terror in enemies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:200
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ogre Kingdoms spells"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:203
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tooth Cracker"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:206
msgid "[.cost]#3+ to cast# [.points]#Range 30cm#"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:211
msgid ""
"_The Butcher grinds his way through a lump of earth encrusted bedrock taken "
"from the peak of a mountain, imbuing himself and his fellows with "
"supernatural resilience. This often costs the Butcher more than a couple of "
"teeth._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:214
msgid ""
"Target friendly unit can’t be driven back or confused until your next turn."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:216
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bone Cruncher"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:224
msgid ""
"_Shovelling dry bones into his mouth, the Butcher painfully crunches his way "
"through femurs, ribs and skulls. As he points at his foes and spits his "
"bloody curse, the enemy find their own bones breaking within their bodies._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:228
msgid ""
"Counts as three shooting attacks with no armour save. The spell causes drive "
"back as for normal shooting. The Wizard must be able to see the target and "
"can’t cast the spell into a combat."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:230
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bull Gorger"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:238
msgid ""
"_The Butcher greedily devours the heart of a Bull Rhinox, no doubt enjoying "
"the feast of healthy blood and muscle whilst he imbues himself and his "
"charges with the strength of a charging Rhinox._"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:242
msgid ""
"The spell adds +1 Attack for each stand in a unit the Butcher has joined, "
"including his own stand. The spell lasts for the duration of the following "
"Combat phase."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:244
#, no-wrap
msgid "Troll Guts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: en/revolution/modules/armies/pages/ogre-kingdoms.adoc:252
msgid ""
